    "b-00-overview-text-5": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-text-5",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "text"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "OWNERSHIP LAYOUT\n\n+----------------------+     +--------------------------+     +----------------------+\n| Scheduler scope      |     | Shared run state         |     | Worker execution     |\n| - run target         |     | - epochs/targets         |---->| - claim A Pi worker  |\n| - indexer output     |<--->| - claims/events          |<----| - claim B Pi worker  |\n| - reducer output     |     | - worker states          |     | - claim N Pi worker  |\n| - epoch policy       |     | - artifacts/wakeups      |     | - PR/docs/source     |\n+----------------------+     | - checkpoints/facts      |     | - experimental       |\n                             +------------+-------------+     |   search             |\n                                          |                   | - permuter handoff   |\n                                          v                   +----------------------+\n                             +------------+-------------+\n                             | Score gate                |\n                             | verify / absorb           |\n                             | refresh baseline          |\n                             +--------------------------+"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-runtime-feedback-loop-caption": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-runtime-feedback-loop-caption",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Runtime feedback loop",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-text-6": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-text-6",
      "type": "process-outline",
      "props": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "run target + report/graph evidence feed the scheduler"
          },
          {
            "text": "Deterministic scheduler — admit/drain/route",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "sends epoch policy to the state substrate; reads wake + snapshot back",
                "kind": "note"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "State substrate — epochs / claims / facts",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "supplies the wake event + snapshot the scheduler reads",
                "kind": "note"
              },
              {
                "text": "emits target packets / claims to the worker pool",
                "kind": "note"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Worker pool — Pi workers under claims, selected capabilities",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "emits checkpoints / events and facts / selected patches",
                "kind": "note"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "State substrate — durable board update",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "emits score candidates",
                "kind": "note"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Score gate — verify / absorb, refresh baseline",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "emits the new baseline",
                "kind": "note"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "refreshed evidence + next board read",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "loops back into the scheduler's next pass",
                "kind": "note"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-the-important-split-is-d-7": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-the-important-split-is-d-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The important split is directional: the scheduler reads durable board state and\nwrites reproducible scheduling transitions; workers receive target claims and\nproduce checkpoint evidence; the state substrate is the only coordination\nsurface between them."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-text-8": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-text-8",
      "type": "process-outline",
      "props": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "Guardian process — waits for incidents"
          },
          {
            "text": "Decomp system — run loop, scheduler, workers",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "process exit / worker error flows back into durable state as an incident packet + recovery",
                "kind": "note"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Durable state — claims/events/logs"
          }
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-the-process-health-loop-9": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-the-process-health-loop-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The process health loop is operational, not strategic. It preserves liveness\naround the decomp system while the scheduler and workers continue to own\ndecompilation decisions."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
